      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\tan\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}-\\theta\\right)&=\\frac{\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}-\\theta\\right)}{\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}-\\theta\\right)}\\\\\\tan\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}-\\theta\\right)&=\\frac{\\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}.\\end{align*}$$\nMary's expression has the same domain as the original: $\\sin\\theta\\ne0$.\n\nAt $\\theta=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$, the original is $\\tan0=0$ and Mary's expression is $\\frac{0}{1}=0$, whereas Bob's expression is undefined because $\\tan\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ is undefined. Bob's form agrees where $\\tan\\theta$ is defined and nonzero, but excludes valid values of the original expression.",
